---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Home">
  <div class="pill-row">
    <p class="pill">PhD Candidate in Bioengineering &middot; UC Berkeley/UCSF</p>
    <p class="pill">Biomaterials &amp; Tissue Regeneration</p>
  </div>
  <h1>Morgan R. Pfaff</h1>
  <p class="tagline">Bioengineer</p>
  <p>
    Hi, I'm Morgan! I've spent the past 10 years designing biomaterials for
    tissue regeneration, from bone grafts to muscle repair. My passion for
    science is closely paralleled by my desire to drive positive change in
    my community, whether that means getting science out of the lab and
    into the clinic or making sure everyone in my community has their basic
    needs met.
  </p>

  <div class="home-cta">
    <a class="btn" href="/research/"><span aria-hidden="true">🌸</span> See My Research</a>
    <a class="btn secondary" href="/about/"><span aria-hidden="true">🌺</span> More About Me</a>
  </div>

  <h2>Right now</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Finishing my PhD</h3>
    <p>
      I'm wrapping up my dissertation in Dr. Kevin Healy's lab in the joint
      UC Berkeley/UCSF Bioengineering program, on viscoelastic,
      semi-synthetic hyaluronic acid hydrogels for soft tissue regeneration.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Moving the work toward the clinic</h3>
    <p>
      I'm a scientific consultant for MuscleMatrix, the startup built partly
      on hydrogel technology I co-invented, helping set up the company from the
      lab bench up.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Teaching and community</h3>
    <p>
      I'm a reader for two Berkeley bioengineering courses and lead a weekly
      meal serve with Food Not Bombs East Bay.
    </p>
  </div>

  <img
    src="/morgan-nu-portrait-hq.jpg"
    alt="Portrait of Morgan R. Pfaff outdoors on Northeastern's campus"
    class="card-img home-photo"
  />
  <p class="photo-credit">Photo by Matthew Modoono/Northeastern University</p>
</Layout>
